{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1435956-storypath-interrogation-torture-mechanics","id":1435956,"title":"[Storypath] Interrogation & torture mechanics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-18T21:15:19-08:00","id":1435956,"title":"[Storypath] Interrogation & torture mechanics","content":"Once again, I would rather put it in the general Storypath subforum - but we do not have it... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> As it's about more mature tropes, I suppose <b>Trinity</b> subforum is better place for it.<br /> <br /> So I did not find rules for interrogation, question and torture in Storypath. I assume this would be some kind of Complex <i>Persuasion</i> Action (?), as there is no <i>Intimidation</i> Skill in Storypath games. Probably rolled against some <i>Integrity</i> Skill pool of the Interrogation target. Taking in the account <b>Scion Dragon </b>intelligence manual part - I would say that <b>until you get 'maximum number of possible rolls' before Milestones, you can get reasonable information</b>. Beyond that, Interrogation target will say anything you want.<br /> <br /> Torture, then, are much nastier way of doing Interrogation rolls - still do not know how it would work then... Like +1 Enhancement on <i>Interrogation</i> roll for each Condition you do on the target, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-18T22:22:34-08:00","id":1435962,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.humanrightsfirst.org/campaigns/never-torture/facts-torture\" target=\"_blank\">Torture is an ineffective method of interrogation</a>. Victims will tell the torturer what they think the torturer wants to hear, rather than giving them useful information.<br /> <br /> Accordingly, I would not give any interrogation-related bonuses for acts of torture.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-18T22:37:11-08:00","id":1435963,"title":"","content":"Interrogation/questioning is covered by the Intrigue mechanics. The person being questioned has an Attitude towards the questioner. The questioner is trying to Influence the other person to encourage their behaviour to answer questions, or discourage them lying. They can also work to shift the person\u2019s Attitude, or alter the environment to shift the Atmosphere.<br /> <br /> Pages 85-90, it\u2019s all there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T00:38:16-08:00","id":1435973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1435956-storypath-interrogation-torture-mechanics?p=1435962#post1435962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.humanrightsfirst.org/campaigns/never-torture/facts-torture&amp;quot;]Torture</a> is an ineffective method of interrogation[/URL]. Victims will tell the torturer what they think the torturer wants to hear, rather than giving them useful information.<br /> <br /> Accordingly, I would not give any interrogation-related bonuses for acts of torture.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Agree 100%","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T03:01:04-08:00","id":1435986,"title":"","content":"My opinion, use the rules for Intrigue. Don\u2019t add enhancements from torture, they don\u2019t help that much and may even have the opposed results.<br /> <br /> If there is physical torture cause some physical conditions, even injury conditions to represent the results, and add some LONG (VERY LONG) behavior conditions related to the traumas caused by it.<br /> <br /> I met people that were tortured by the dictatorship in Brazil (1964-1984) and they acted normal until some thing triggered their traumas (20+ years after their being tortured). Even those not physically tortured, locked in small rooms for days, listening to people being tortured, etc, like what happens to people that went to war, have long term impact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T11:31:52-08:00","id":1436049,"title":"","content":"In the real world the closest torture has come to providing reliable intelligence is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forced_confession\" target=\"_blank\">forced confessions</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Senate_Intelligence_Committee_report_on_CIA_torture#Misleading_information_provided_by_the_CIA\" target=\"_blank\">signal intelligence being passed off as coming from torture</a> in order to justify it's continued use. If your goal is to emulate the actually effectiveness of torture it should be a penalty, possibly to the point of acting as an automatic failure in your intelligence gathering.<br /> <br /> If you're trying to achieve some other goal with rules I think you need to be more clear with what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T13:41:25-08:00","id":1436069,"title":"","content":"Torture tends to cause <a href=\"https://www.verywellmind.com/confabulation-definition-examples-and-treatments-4177450\" target=\"_blank\">confabulation</a>, which basically just corrupts whatever information the victim had. Not only is it a horrific thing to do, but it's also a stupid thing to do unless you're just a sadist doing it for kicks, a total asshole trying to scare people, or looking to get a false confession on record.<br /> <br /> That's why even superheroes with lie detection powers (like Netflix's Daredevil) shouldn't try to use it. The victim won't even realize they're not telling the truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T14:24:56-08:00","id":1436074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1435956-storypath-interrogation-torture-mechanics?p=1436069#post1436069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why even superheroes with lie detection powers (like Netflix's Daredevil) shouldn't try to use it. The victim won't even realize they're not telling the truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a really important fact, the victim at some point do believe in the true they are telling, even if it was never true, so even a Mega perceptive Nova or a Telepath Psion will detect it as true.<br /> <br /> A deep probe in the memories will show they were altered, probably, but the superficial thoughts will be faithful to the \u201ctrue told\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T18:55:11-08:00","id":1436119,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about the question of torture in game more and I think the way I'd handle it, if my players really wanted to do it, would be to apply a Complication with level equal to the injury conditions inflicted. If the PC's can't (or don't) buy of the Complication the information they gain is tailored to whatever their victim thinks they want to hear and is dangerously flawed. Maybe half the intelligence is just lies, maybe important details are added or omitted that might lead to problems down the line.<br /> <br /> For example, trying to torture the location of fellow rebels out of a prisoner might lead them to describe a hospital where some staff members look the other way when providing treatment as a dangerous training facility filled with rebel fighters. Should the PC's take the intelligence at face value they are likely to go in utterly over-armed and suffer a public relations hit at best or commit war crimes at worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T21:49:25-08:00","id":1436147,"title":"","content":"edit: I think I misread the post I was responding to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T08:52:00-08:00","id":1436213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1435956-storypath-interrogation-torture-mechanics?p=1436069#post1436069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Torture tends to cause <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://www.verywellmind.com/confabulation-definition-examples-and-treatments-4177450&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">confabulation</a>, which basically just corrupts whatever information the victim had. Not only is it a horrific thing to do, but it's also a stupid thing to do unless you're just a sadist doing it for kicks, a total asshole trying to scare people, or looking to get a false confession on record.<br /> <br /> That's why even superheroes with lie detection powers (like Netflix's Daredevil) shouldn't try to use it. The victim won't even realize they're not telling the truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow! Idk that. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T12:55:27-08:00","id":1436266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1435956-storypath-interrogation-torture-mechanics?p=1435962#post1435962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.humanrightsfirst.org/campaigns/never-torture/facts-torture&amp;quot;]Torture</a> is an ineffective method of interrogation[/URL]. Victims will tell the torturer what they think the torturer wants to hear, rather than giving them useful information.<br /> <br /> Accordingly, I would not give any interrogation-related bonuses for acts of torture.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have wrestled with the question of whether Talents should have a Gift that makes torture work, since torture works for pulp heroes in much of the media Talents draw on. I decided though that that particular trope, like the racism in much of the media that Adventure! draws on is better rejected than emulated since shaking the public belief that is a real thing is so important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T15:18:56-08:00","id":1436295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1435956-storypath-interrogation-torture-mechanics?p=1436266#post1436266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have wrestled with the question of whether Talents should have a Gift that makes torture work, since torture works for pulp heroes in much of the media Talents draw on. I decided though that that particular trope, like the racism in much of the media that Adventure! draws on is better rejected than emulated since shaking the public belief that is a real thing is so important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, <i>depicting</i> torture as something that's effective seems to have <i>convinced</i> some people that torture is effective; there's some disturbing statistics out there about how <i>24</i> impacted the beliefs of Americans.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T15:35:41-08:00","id":1436304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1435956-storypath-interrogation-torture-mechanics?p=1436295#post1436295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, <i>depicting</i> torture as something that's effective seems to have <i>convinced</i> some people that torture is effective; there's some disturbing statistics out there about how <i>24</i> impacted the beliefs of Americans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, I agree with both of you guys. I\u2019ve seen that thing about how torture really does work repeated as fact in novels too. I\u2019m glad Storypath rejected that particular trope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}